# Opposing Force M249 SAW. Measured by vrcardgen, finished by hand.
#
# Part K: "Belt-fed: open the top cover (hinge), lay the belt on the feed
# tray from the box, close the cover, pull the charging handle. The heaviest
# gun in the game."
#
# The other mechanism that exists nowhere in stock Half-Life, and the model
# has all of it: `Object05` is the charging handle at 17.49 units - the plan
# quotes 17.5 - `Object02` is the top cover, turning 1.675 radians and only
# in `reload1`, and `saw_clipbox` is the ammunition box.
#
# A BELT IS A QUEUE, which is what a tube is, so the simulator carries it as
# one. What makes it a belt rather than a magazine is the cover: rounds go in
# only while it is open, and none come out while it is. A SAW with the cover
# up does not fire, which is the whole reason you can see the belt.

weapon v_saw
match  bones 41  seqs 9  hash 0x99236238

# The bone every position in this card is measured in - the controls, the
# grab points, the chamber, the ejection port. Nothing recorded it until
# the engine had to place a control in the world to ask whether a thumb is
# near it; the simulator never needed one, because it never works in world
# space. Taken from the generator, which has always called this bone the
# WEAPON BODY and is what measured these numbers in the first place.
body   "box_04"

type   belt  capacity 50  rpm 800
fire   auto  rpm 800

# The charging handle.
joint 0  bone "Object05"  slide  travel 17.49  rest 0
    grab  point 0.00 0.00 0.00  radius 3.0

# The top cover. It stays where it is put - a cover has a detent, not a
# spring, which is why it carries no return.
joint 1  bone "Object02"  hinge  travel 1.68  rest 0
    # Near shut rather than half way: cover_open is latched from this
    # crossing, and at half travel its hysteresis band is where a hand
    # that half-closes the cover leaves it - reading shut while the
    # cover is visibly up. Anything not seated is open for loading.
    point cover_open at 0.12
    grab  point 0.00 0.00 0.00  radius 3.5

# `saw_clipbox` is the ammunition box and `v_saw_round1..5` are the belt
# itself. Neither is a joint: the box is a thing you take a belt out of and
# the rounds are what the feed path owns.
